    failing check, aligned the same way as the main table: service, check name, detail. Rows follow the snapshot's order
    of services and checks. A missing [38;5;153mdetail[39m prints as blank. When nothing is failing, the section is left out, so a
    healthy environment's output is the table plus the new column.
  - [38;5;153mbin/svc.js[39m, [38;5;153msrc/load.js[39m and the snapshot format stay the same. I'll add one line to the README's Usage section
    describing the new column and section.

